{
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**The problem.** Balloons in a row have numbers `nums[i]`. Bursting balloon `i` earns `left · nums[i] · right`, where `left` and `right` are its **current** neighbours (a missing neighbour counts as 1); then it's gone and its neighbours become adjacent. Burst them all. Return the **most coins** you can collect."
    },
    {
      "type": "drawing",
      "src": "/drawings/f1538bf4-298a-4214-a21e-ea185a3ea5b0.svg",
      "alt": "nums is 3, 1, 5, 8, padded with a 1 at each end. The best order bursts 1, 5, 3, 8 for 15 + 120 + 24 + 8 = 167 coins. Thinking backwards: 8 is the last balloon of the whole range, earning 1 times 8 times 1; inside the range from the left wall to 8, the 3 bursts last, earning 1 times 3 times 8. best(l, r) tries every balloon k between l and r as the last one: best(l, k) plus vals[l] times vals[k] times vals[r] plus best(k, r).",
      "width": 757,
      "height": 423,
      "scene": {
