    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Example"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "text",
      "code": "nums = [3, 1, 5, 8]  ->  167   (burst 1, 5, 3, 8)\nnums = [1, 5]        ->  10    (burst 1: 1*1*5, then 5: 1*5*1)\nnums = [7]           ->  7"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "The idea: think about the last balloon, not the first"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "The obvious recursion picks the **first** balloon to burst. But then its two neighbours become adjacent, so the left part and the right part are no longer separate problems — the state would have to be *the whole set of balloons left*, 2ⁿ of them."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Flip it: pick the balloon `k` that bursts **last** in a range. While `k` is still standing, it separates the balloons on its left from those on its right — they never become neighbours, so the two sides really are **independent**. And when `k` finally bursts, everything between `l` and `r` is gone, so its neighbours are exactly `l` and `r`. Pad the row with a 1 at each end, and let `best(l, r)` be the most coins from bursting every balloon **strictly between** `l` and `r`:"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "text",
      "code": "best(l, r) = max over l < k < r of   best(l, k) + vals[l] * vals[k] * vals[r] + best(k, r)\nbest(l, r) = 0 when nothing is between them (r - l < 2)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "This is the hardest kind of interval DP: instead of shrinking from the ends, it tries every **split point** inside the range."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "1. Memoized recursion"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "javascript",
      "code": "function maxCoins(nums) {\n  const vals = [1, ...nums, 1];                  // a 1 at each end: bursting next to a wall\n  const memo = new Map();\n  const best = (l, r) => {                       // most coins for the balloons strictly between l and r\n    if (r - l < 2) return 0;                     // nothing between them\n    const key = l * vals.length + r;\n    if (memo.has(key)) return memo.get(key);\n    let most = 0;\n    for (let k = l + 1; k < r; k++) {            // k is the LAST balloon burst between l and r\n      most = Math.max(most, best(l, k) + vals[l] * vals[k] * vals[r] + best(k, r));\n    }\n    memo.set(key, most);\n    return most;\n  };\n  return best(0, vals.length - 1);\n}"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "python",
      "code": "from functools import cache\n\ndef max_coins(nums):\n    vals = [1] + nums + [1]               # a 1 at each end: bursting next to a wall\n\n    @cache\n    def best(l, r):                       # most coins for the balloons strictly between l and r\n        most = 0\n        for k in range(l + 1, r):         # k is the LAST balloon burst between l and r\n            most = max(most, best(l, k) + vals[l] * vals[k] * vals[r] + best(k, r))\n        return most\n\n    return best(0, len(vals) - 1)"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "java",
      "code": "int[] vals;\nInteger[][] memo;\n\nint maxCoins(int[] nums) {\n    int m = nums.length + 2;\n    vals = new int[m];\n    vals[0] = vals[m - 1] = 1;                   // a 1 at each end: bursting next to a wall\n    for (int i = 0; i < nums.length; i++) vals[i + 1] = nums[i];\n    memo = new Integer[m][m];\n    return best(0, m - 1);\n}\n\nint best(int l, int r) {                         // most coins for the balloons strictly between l and r\n    if (r - l < 2) return 0;                     // nothing between them\n    if (memo[l][r] != null) return memo[l][r];\n    int most = 0;\n    for (int k = l + 1; k < r; k++) {            // k is the LAST balloon burst between l and r\n        most = Math.max(most, best(l, k) + vals[l] * vals[k] * vals[r] + best(k, r));\n    }\n    memo[l][r] = most;\n    return most;\n}"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "cpp",
      "code": "vector<int> vals;\nvector<vector<int>> memo;                        // -1 = not solved yet\n\nint best(int l, int r) {                         // most coins for the balloons strictly between l and r\n    if (r - l < 2) return 0;                     // nothing between them\n    int& m = memo[l][r];\n    if (m != -1) return m;\n    int most = 0;\n    for (int k = l + 1; k < r; k++) {            // k is the LAST balloon burst between l and r\n        most = max(most, best(l, k) + vals[l] * vals[k] * vals[r] + best(k, r));\n    }\n    return m = most;\n}\n\nint maxCoins(vector<int>& nums) {\n    vals = {1};                                  // a 1 at each end: bursting next to a wall\n    vals.insert(vals.end(), nums.begin(), nums.end());\n    vals.push_back(1);\n    memo.assign(vals.size(), vector<int>(vals.size(), -1));\n    return best(0, vals.size() - 1);\n}"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**Time O(n³), space O(n²).** There are O(n²) ranges and each tries O(n) last balloons. The recursion is only O(n) deep, since every call shrinks the range."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "2. Bottom-up, shortest ranges first"
    },
    {
      "type": "simulator",
      "program": "burst-balloons-table",
      "caption": "Fill ranges from short to long; each range tries every balloon inside it as the last to burst."
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "javascript",
      "code": "function maxCoins(nums) {\n  const vals = [1, ...nums, 1];\n  const m = vals.length;\n  // dp[l][r]: most coins for bursting every balloon strictly between l and r\n  const dp = Array.from({ length: m }, () => new Array(m).fill(0));\n  for (let gap = 2; gap < m; gap++) {            // shorter ranges first\n    for (let l = 0; l + gap < m; l++) {\n      const r = l + gap;\n      for (let k = l + 1; k < r; k++) {          // k bursts last, between l and r\n        dp[l][r] = Math.max(dp[l][r], dp[l][k] + vals[l] * vals[k] * vals[r] + dp[k][r]);\n      }\n    }\n  }\n  return dp[0][m - 1];\n}"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "python",
      "code": "def max_coins(nums):\n    vals = [1] + nums + [1]\n    m = len(vals)\n    # dp[l][r]: most coins for bursting every balloon strictly between l and r\n    dp = [[0] * m for _ in range(m)]\n    for gap in range(2, m):               # shorter ranges first\n        for l in range(m - gap):\n            r = l + gap\n            for k in range(l + 1, r):     # k bursts last, between l and r\n                dp[l][r] = max(dp[l][r], dp[l][k] + vals[l] * vals[k] * vals[r] + dp[k][r])\n    return dp[0][m - 1]"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "java",
      "code": "int maxCoins(int[] nums) {\n    int m = nums.length + 2;\n    int[] vals = new int[m];\n    vals[0] = vals[m - 1] = 1;\n    for (int i = 0; i < nums.length; i++) vals[i + 1] = nums[i];\n    int[][] dp = new int[m][m];                  // dp[l][r]: most coins for the balloons strictly between l and r\n    for (int gap = 2; gap < m; gap++) {          // shorter ranges first\n        for (int l = 0; l + gap < m; l++) {\n            int r = l + gap;\n            for (int k = l + 1; k < r; k++) {    // k bursts last, between l and r\n                dp[l][r] = Math.max(dp[l][r], dp[l][k] + vals[l] * vals[k] * vals[r] + dp[k][r]);\n            }\n        }\n    }\n    return dp[0][m - 1];\n}"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "cpp",
      "code": "int maxCoins(vector<int>& nums) {\n    vector<int> vals = {1};\n    vals.insert(vals.end(), nums.begin(), nums.end());\n    vals.push_back(1);\n    int m = vals.size();\n    vector<vector<int>> dp(m, vector<int>(m, 0)); // dp[l][r]: most coins for the balloons strictly between l and r\n    for (int gap = 2; gap < m; gap++) {          // shorter ranges first\n        for (int l = 0; l + gap < m; l++) {\n            int r = l + gap;\n            for (int k = l + 1; k < r; k++) {    // k bursts last, between l and r\n                dp[l][r] = max(dp[l][r], dp[l][k] + vals[l] * vals[k] * vals[r] + dp[k][r]);\n            }\n        }\n    }\n    return dp[0][m - 1];\n}"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**Time O(n³), space O(n²).** Every `dp[l][k]` and `dp[k][r]` covers a shorter range than `dp[l][r]`, so filling by increasing `gap` guarantees they're ready. With LeetCode's `n ≤ 300` that's about 4.5 million steps — fast."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Comparing the approaches"
    },
    {
      "type": "complexity",
      "rows": [
        {
          "approach": "Memoized recursion",
          "time": "O(n³)",
          "timeWhy": "**O(n²)** ranges, and each tries **O(n)** balloons as the last one burst.",
          "space": "O(n²)",
          "spaceWhy": "One memo entry **per range**; the recursion itself is only O(n) deep."
        },
        {
          "approach": "Bottom-up, shortest ranges first",
          "time": "O(n³)",
          "timeWhy": "The same **n²** ranges × **n** last-balloon choices, filled by increasing length.",
          "space": "O(n²)",
          "spaceWhy": "The **n × n** table of ranges."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "The brute force — try every burst order — is O(n!), and choosing the *first* balloon gives no clean subproblems. The whole problem is the insight that the *last* balloon splits the range cleanly; say that first, and the code follows."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Edge cases to test"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "ordered": false,
      "items": [
        "**One balloon** — `[7]`: 1 · 7 · 1 = 7.",
        "**Zeros** — a 0 balloon earns nothing and is best burst early, so its neighbours meet.",
        "**Equal values** — `[2, 2, 2]`: 2·2·2 + 1·2·2 + 1·2·1 = 8 + 4 + 2 = 14.",
        "**Forgetting the padding** — the walls count as 1, not 0."
      ]
    },
